  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find IB and IGCSE tutors in Malegaon?", answer: "Send IB Gram your child's programme, subject, level and target exam session; we shortlist tutors who have actually taught that exact course. Location plays no role in the shortlist, since nothing local exists in Malegaon anyway, so syllabus fit decides everything. A free trial online comes before any commitment, and a different tutor gets suggested if the first pairing is not right." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE home tutors in Malegaon for Cambridge and Edexcel?", answer: "Both boards are covered, delivered as live online home tuition rather than a home visit. Cambridge candidates get matched by syllabus code and tier, Mathematics 0580 Extended or Biology 0610 for instance, and Edexcel candidates by specification and Foundation or Higher tier, each working from that board's own current papers." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Malegaon?", answer: "They do not. Home visits exist only in Gurugram and a few Delhi NCR pockets; nowhere else in India, including Malegaon, does a tutor call at the door. What happens instead is a live online lesson, one to one, with a shared digital whiteboard doing the work an in-person visit otherwise would, delivered right to your home over video." },
    { question: "Is there any IB or IGCSE school in Malegaon?", answer: "No. Every school inside Malegaon follows the Maharashtra State Board, taught in Urdu, Marathi or English medium; none teaches the IB or a Cambridge or Pearson Edexcel IGCSE syllabus. Families set on either curriculum use Cambridge's private-candidate exam system through Mumbai, or arrange boarding at a school in Pune or Mumbai." },
    { question: "What is the private-candidate route for IGCSE, and does it actually work from Malegaon?", answer: "Cambridge lets a student who has never attended a Cambridge school register as a private candidate and sit the official exam at an approved centre, often through the British Council or a recognised school such as RIMS International School in Mumbai. Study happens online from Malegaon; travel is needed only for the exam series itself, provided registration is sorted well in advance." },
    { question: "Can my child study for the IB Diploma from Malegaon the same way?", answer: "No, not through a private-candidate route, because none exists for the Diploma. It requires full enrolment at an authorised IB World School, so a Malegaon family set specifically on the Diploma is really looking at boarding in a city such as Pune or Mumbai rather than online-only study." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor in Malegaon cost?", answer: "The programme, subject, session length and how recently a tutor has taught that exact syllabus all move the rate, which gets fixed before the trial and stays that way afterward. Diploma Higher Level subjects generally cost more than MYP or IGCSE Core work. Online delivery removes any travel charge, and nothing runs on a long contract, so stopping or pausing is straightforward." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial class before I commit?", answer: "Yes, always. Your child works through a genuine topic from their own syllabus with the tutor online, free of charge and with no strings attached. A short plan for month one follows, and from there you choose to continue, ask for changes, or try someone else." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments for a Malegaon student?", answer: "Tutors guide the IA process without writing any of it themselves: helping settle on a workable research question, unpacking what a criterion is actually asking for, planning data collection, and reviewing drafts honestly. Anything that involves writing or rewriting the assessed piece breaches IB integrity rules, so it simply does not happen." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you help with for a Malegaon student?", answer: "The major DP subject groups that come up for students boarding away from Malegaon are covered: both Maths strands at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management and English A most commonly, plus Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay support." },
    { question: "Do you tutor IB MYP and PYP students connected to Malegaon, not only the Diploma?", answer: "The full continuum is covered, not just the Diploma. MYP sessions focus on criterion-based writing in the sciences and languages and on the Personal Project's process journal; PYP sessions build reading, writing, number confidence and the early research skills the Exhibition eventually needs, in short, regular online slots." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring genuinely effective given Malegaon has no local alternative?", answer: "Given there is nothing local to compare it against for a Higher Level IB subject or a specific IGCSE code, it works well by default. A shared whiteboard, screen-shared past papers and recorded worked examples replace nearly everything a tutor sitting beside a student would otherwise do, while opening the field to genuine specialists anywhere in India." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors verified for Malegaon students?", answer: "Qualifications, how recently a tutor has taught the exact subject and level, and their handling of assessment criteria all get checked before any introduction to a family. Since there is no local school to draw a tutor pool from, the bar is genuine recent experience with that syllabus, not confident generalism. The free trial then lets you confirm that yourself." },
    { question: "When should a Malegaon student start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Right at the start of the course is cleanest: Class 11 for the Diploma, Grade 9 for IGCSE, leaving time to fix gaps before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades hit. A later start, even in the final year, can still help meaningfully if tutoring stays narrowly focused on the highest-value topics and past papers." },
    { question: "My child is moving from the Maharashtra State Board to IB or IGCSE. Can an online tutor help from Malegaon?", answer: "Yes, and it is a common request, since nothing local runs either curriculum from the start. Content is rarely the gap; exam style is. Words like 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' need direct teaching, along with new habits around IA or coursework planning, ideally started well ahead of the actual switch." },
    { question: "Can sessions happen on weekends or after school hours for a Malegaon family?", answer: "Weekday evenings after school and weekend mornings are what most families book. Scheduling works around the city's severe pre-monsoon heat, when an earlier slot is often preferred, and around Ramzan, when many households run a different daily rhythm for the month. A second weekly slot before mocks or an exam sitting is easy to add." },
    { question: "What happens if we are not happy with the tutor?", answer: "Say so, and a different tutor gets found. Reviews happen with families every few weeks precisely so a mismatch does not linger, and no child is expected to stick with someone who is not working out. Nothing here runs on a long contract, so pausing or stopping costs nothing either." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any school, or with the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "No. IB Gram operates independently, with no affiliation to any school, to the International Baccalaureate Organization, to Cambridge Assessment International Education, or to Pearson Edexcel. Any school mentioned on this page simply illustrates a genuine route into these curricula, and tutors follow that school's calendar and the relevant board's published syllabus." },
  ],

